---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About · James Samuel-Camps"
  description="Lead Product Designer with over 15 years experience building complex B2B/B2C fintech infrastructure, design systems, and UI architecture."
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="about-header">
      <h1 class="about-quote">
        “I will fight you one of these days.”
      </h1>
      <p class="about-cite">— Product Manager, YouLend</p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <p class="about-standfirst statement">
        I’m a Lead Product Designer with over 15 years of experience building complex B2B/B2C fintech infrastructure, design systems, and scalable UI architecture. Currently based in the UK, open to new opportunities, and building <a href="https://github.com/jamessamuelcamps/tilia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tilia</a>, a free UX research platform for solo practitioners, small product teams, and founders.
      </p>

      <section class="about-row">
        <div class="about-row-band">
          <span class="about-row-num">01 —</span>
        </div>
        <div class="about-row-head">
          <h2 class="about-row-title">Background & Mindset</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="about-row-body prose">
          <p>
            My path into product design wasn’t standard. I studied magazine journalism, spending my early career in trend forecasting and editorial design. That background taught me two critical skills that define my approach today:
          </p>
          <ul class="about-highlights statement-list">
            <li>Separating long-term human behaviour from short-term fads</li>
            <li>Mastering strict information hierarchy</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            In fintech, where software is often weighed down by legacy code and heavy regulatory constraints, I use those skills to abstract messy logic into simple, intuitive user mental models.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-row">
        <div class="about-row-band">
          <span class="about-row-num">02 —</span>
        </div>
        <div class="about-row-head">
          <h2 class="about-row-title">Approach to Leadership</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="about-row-body prose">
          <p>
            I’m passionate about mentoring and supporting my team, with a strong belief in trust-based management. I trust that you’re here on merit and that you know how to do the job well. I can’t be across every project at all times, so I count on you to keep me updated, and to say early when you need support or a second opinion.
          </p>
          <p>
            While I see myself as accountable for my team’s development, I encourage them to take charge of their own paths, with me providing guidance as needed. My feedback style is adaptable; happy with async, but I prefer real-time for in-depth discussions.
          </p>
          <ul class="about-highlights statement-list">
            <li>My default setting is trust</li>
            <li>Micromanagement stifles growth and never leads to the desired results</li>
            <li>I expect my team to help shape their own path, not be handed one</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-row">
        <div class="about-row-band">
          <span class="about-row-num">03 —</span>
        </div>
        <div class="about-row-head">
          <h2 class="about-row-title">How I Operate</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="about-row-body prose">
          <h3>Logic over Theatre</h3>
          <p>
            I value outcomes over performative design rituals. I prefer fast, informed assumptions, quick prototypes, and immediate testing over endless “design by committee.” Process should serve product velocity, not slow it down.
          </p>

          <h3>Systems Architecture</h3>
          <p>
            I am drawn to the structural layer of product design. I turn back-end technical complexity into clear, maintainable design systems and self-service component libraries. Solid documentation and UI systems are business assets that save hundreds of engineering hours.
          </p>

          <h3>Autonomy, Trust & Momentum</h3>
          <p>
            I believe in tight, cross-functional alignment early on; aligning with product, risk, and engineering on what needs to be solved. Once aligned, I execute with high autonomy and protect the team’s maker-time so we can focus on shipping high-quality software quickly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-header {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-16);
  }

  .about-quote {
    font-size: var(--font-size-4xl);
    line-height: var(--line-height-tight);
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about-quote {
      font-size: var(--font-size-7xl);
    }
  }

  .about-cite {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* Centred 12-col container; the label + copy columns sit inset from both edges */
  .about-grid {
    --section-gap: calc(var(--space-16) + var(--space-8));
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
    column-gap: var(--gutter);
    row-gap: 0;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  /* .statement / .statement-list carry the type treatment (see global.css) */
  /* Lead paragraph: statement type, but without the em-dash marker */
  .about-standfirst {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    margin-bottom: var(--section-gap);
    padding-left: 0;
  }

  .about-standfirst::before {
    content: none;
  }

  .about-standfirst a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .about-highlights {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  .about-row {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: subgrid;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .about-row + .about-row {
    margin-top: var(--section-gap);
  }

  /* Number band — its own full-width row above the two columns, with a
     stroke beneath. Mirrors .cs-section-band on the case studies. */
  .about-row-band {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .about-row-head {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-row-num {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .about-row-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-row-body {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .about-row-body,
  .about-row-body p {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .about-row-body > :first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .about-row-body > :last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about-grid {
      --section-gap: calc(var(--space-24) + var(--space-6));
    }

    .about-standfirst {
      grid-column: 1 / 11;
      font-size: var(--font-size-3xl);
    }

    .about-row-head {
      grid-column: 1 / 4;
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .about-row-body {
      grid-column: 4 / 11;
    }
  }
</style>
